 of the Homeland Security Act of 2002 by adding a new statutory prohibition section regarding information sharing and Trusted Traveler programs.","evidence":"Title VII of the Homeland Security Act of 2002 (6 U.S.C. 341 et seq.) is amended by adding at the end the following new section","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":40},{"assessment":"Establishes permanent restrictions on Department of Homeland Security data access and program administration.","evidence":null,"evidence_verified":false,"key":"duration","score":70}],"missing_information":["Any authorized appropriations or financial costs associated with complying with the data-sharing prohibitions.","Operational impact details on specific data systems currently utilized by ICE and CBP."],"rationale":"The bill prohibits the Department of Homeland Security from using TSA data or specific private sector passenger data broker information for CBP and ICE functions, and protects Trusted Traveler program enrollment from being terminated based on First Amendment-protected activities.","score":40},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-11-04T22:43:46+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr10040/BILLS-119hr10040ih.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2026-08-03","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 10040","latest_action":{"date":"2026-08-04","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security."},"members":[{"chamber":"House","district":"12","id":"T000481","name":"Rep. Tlaib, Rashida","party":"D","role":"sponsor","state":"MI"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2026-08-03","district":"3","id":"A000381","name":"Rep. Ansari, Yassamin","original":true,"party":"D","role":"cosponsor","state":"AZ"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2026-08-03","district":"7","id":"C001072","name":"Rep. Carson, André","original":true,"party":"D","role":"cosponsor","state":"IN"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2026-08-03","district":"7","id":"F000468","name":"Rep. Fletcher, L